LGPL only: VLC's GPL-2+ modules and Lua stay out of libvlc.so, and the Lua scripts out of the package

VLC's LGPL switch (`--license l`) picks the contribs; VLC's own modules are compiled whatever it
says. A licence scan of every source file behind the package's module list (21.11.2026) found these
GPL-2.0-or-later modules in libvlc.so: dummy (control/dummy.c), file_logger (logger/file.c), hqdn3d
(video_filter/hqdn3d.h), rc (control/cli/), rotate (video_filter/rotate.c, control/motionlib.c),
stream_out_cycle (stream_out/cycle.c), stream_out_rtp (stream_out/rtp.c), syslog (logger/syslog.c),
and lua (all of modules/lua/). The package also carried VLC's Lua scripts as assets: 27 of its 29
are GPL-2+, and only the lua module reads them.

- build-libvlc.sh: `--disable-lua` in both lists (contribs, VLC's configure); the eight modules join
  the module blacklist (sap is on it already).
- libvlc/build.gradle: no Lua scripts copied into the package's assets (the HRTF file stays).

Cobi Player uses none of them: it passes no option that names them, and plays direct stream URLs
(no Lua playlist parser). Yadif, FFmpeg's GPL line filter inside the LGPL deinterlace plugin, goes
with our VLC patch 9007. android/libvlc/check.sh refuses a package with any of it.

--- a/buildsystem/build-libvlc.sh
+++ b/buildsystem/build-libvlc.sh
@@ -301,7 +301,7 @@ VLC_CONTRIB_ARGS="\
     --enable-libarchive \
     --enable-libdsm \
     --enable-libplacebo \
-    --enable-lua \
+    --disable-lua \
     --enable-microdns \
     --enable-mpg123 \
     --enable-nfs \
@@ -361,7 +361,7 @@ VLC_CONFIGURE_ARGS="\
     --enable-jpeg \
     --enable-libass \
     --enable-libxml2 \
-    --enable-lua \
+    --disable-lua \
     --enable-matroska \
     --enable-mod \
     --enable-mpg123 \
@@ -431,6 +431,19 @@ VLC_MODULE_BLACKLIST="
     yuv
     .dummy
 "
+# Cobi Player: VLC's GPL-2+ modules stay out, whatever the licence switch says: this libVLC
+# ships under the LGPL only. Lua (GPL-2+ too, and its scripts) is off in both configure lists.
+# sap is above already. Scripts/check-engine-gpl-free.sh refuses an engine with any of them.
+VLC_MODULE_BLACKLIST="${VLC_MODULE_BLACKLIST}
+    dummy
+    file_logger
+    hqdn3d
+    rc
+    rotate
+    stream_out_cycle
+    stream_out_rtp
+    syslog
+"
 
